KNOWNBUG
wire_array_structs1.sv
--aig --bound 1
^\[main\.p0\] .*: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p1\] .*: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^Invariant check failed$
--
The netlist converter leaves the definitions of the elements of an array
of structs unsplit. The aig engine then refutes p0, and fails a
precondition in bitstring_to_expr when it builds the counterexample. The
same holds on main.
